  "title": "Contents: Banda Bahadur and the Khalsa Struggle",
  "blocks": [
    {
      "id": "manual-6-1",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "This contents page continues the Volume I table of contents and functions as navigation metadata rather than narrative. It gathers the later Banda Bahadur sequence, beginning with Seharkhand, Salodi, Samana, Sadhaura, Wazir Khan, and Malerkotla."
    },
    {
      "id": "manual-6-2",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "The middle entries point readers toward Doaba, the Singhs of Salodi, Banda Singh blessing Deep Singh, Mughal anxiety at Banda Singh’s rise, and the hill-state episodes involving Kebloor, Mandi, Kullu, and Chamba."
    },
    {
      "id": "manual-6-3",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "The final cluster lists the Bahadur Shah, Chistodian, Jaali Din, Shamas Khan, Baizid Khan, last Banda Singh, Tat Khalsa, Mughal conspiracy, Khalsa, and factional-fight episodes. The repair makes the contents page browsable without pretending it is story prose."
    }
  ],
